nter dereference in the NOOP re-proposal branch and leaves the instance uncommitted. The map now records the unguarded dereference in B6 and an overview open detail with the bounded inference that the panic ends the process because the run loop has no recover.\\\",\n  \\\"remaining\\\":[\\\"the history that leaves a restarted owner holding a message-created record for its own instance, which the check fixes as two messages rather than constructing\\\",\n    \\\"the client-side consequence of the same NOOP recovery (the active client-completion candidate)\\\",\n    \\\"the open scope-issue bookkeeping on the superseded C1 artifact\\\"],\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Recording the confirmed crash at the coordinates where the branch lives keeps the map usable for the next question without promoting the finding into the map's own verdict: the claim and its check remain the home for the confirmed result.\\\",\n  \\\"understanding\\\":\\\"updated\\\",\\\"question_updates\\\":{}}}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-map-c4.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-map-c4.json 2>&1 | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
